<h2 class="wp-block-heading tf-title">Questions <span class="tf-sub">Care at home, orders and the shop</span></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>How long should I expect my cut flowers to last in a vase?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We believe in being entirely honest about cut flower longevity: cut stems usually last 5–7 days, though the exact duration depends on the flower variety, room warmth, and water care. Tender petals like sweet peas or ranunculus will often finish their cycle within five days, whereas hardy branches, foliage, and garden roses may hold their fresh appearance well past a week. Keeping flowers in a cool spot and refreshing the water every two days will ensure you enjoy their full, natural lifespan.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>How should I condition and trim stems when I bring flowers home?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you unpack your flowers, fill a thoroughly cleaned vase with fresh, cool tap water. Using a sharp knife or clean floral snips, trim approximately two centimetres from the base of each stem at a clean angle. Always strip away any lower leaves that would otherwise sit below the water level, as submerged foliage decomposes quickly and introduces bacteria. Place the stems into the vase immediately after cutting so water absorption begins without air bubbles blocking the stems.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>How often should I change the water in my flower vase?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We recommend changing your vase water completely every two days. Pour out the old water, rinse the vase thoroughly to remove any bacterial film, and refill with clean, cool water. Each time you refresh the vase, trim a few millimetres from the stem ends to reopen the water channels. This simple two-minute routine is the single most effective way to keep your flowers vibrant and prevent premature drooping of delicate flower heads.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>Where in my home should I display my flower arrangement?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Position your arrangement in a cool area out of direct sunlight, strong draughts, and heating radiators. Direct heat will rapidly dehydrate delicate petals and cause buds to open and fade too quickly. Additionally, keep flowers away from fruit bowls containing apples or bananas, as ripening fruit releases ethylene gas that accelerates wilting. A quiet side table, kitchen counter, or dining board with gentle ambient daylight is the ideal setting.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>What are your workshop opening hours and visit days?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our shop at 14 Linden Row in Aldmere is open Tuesday through Saturday from 9:00 to 18:00, and on Sunday from 10:00 to 15:00. We are closed on Monday for our weekly market trips and workroom stem conditioning. You are always welcome to stop by during open hours to choose loose stems, pick up pre-ordered table posies, or discuss flower requirements for upcoming family ceremonies.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>What are your delivery areas and fee policies?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We deliver across Aldmere within an 8 km radius of our Linden Row workshop for an €8 flat delivery charge. For orders placed Tuesday through Saturday before 12:00, we provide same-day delivery service. Orders placed after noon or on our closed Monday will be scheduled for delivery on the following business day. Lin Wei personally coordinates each delivery route to make sure your flowers arrive in prime condition.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details tf-faq__item"><summary>How does the weekly household subscription work and can I pause it?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
